#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""FS3 v159 - fixes and wishes from the v158 tests.

    Fire     the delay between pressing fire and the shot is gone. Since
             v157 the dorsal-turret line sat between the fire check and the
             cooldown on release, so the cooldown only ran while the button
             was held (Dante 0.39 s late). Every primary of the player.
    Loader   a wide, flat bar of twenty slanted segments across the box,
             no gloss, no rounding; corner brackets like the game windows;
             only the segment being filled glows; percent left, MB right.
    Hold     a held secondary button (right mouse, SEC button) fires again
             as soon as the launcher is ready. A flying Infyrno is only set
             off by a fresh press.
    Racks    Herc Mk II 30 and Ares 32 secondaries (FreeSpace banks,
             Hercules 120 = 20).
    Perseus  player hull in the NTF cycle (open at 2000 points), escort
             and NTF enemy. The hangar closes its gaps when nine hulls are
             open.
    Turrets  capital ship guns cover the full circle: the heavy enemy round
             and the salvo of ships without mounts are aimed, escort
             capital ships fire behind them as well.
    Bursts   Dante, Infyrno and flak shrapnel no longer fly as a perfect
             star: pieces vary in direction, speed, reach and size, now
             and then one more or less, the damage of a burst stays.

Needs v158. Edits src/10_core.js, src/30_waves.js, src/40_world.js,
src/50_combat.js, src/55_arms.js, src/60_effects.js, src/70_ui.js and
loader.html in place, and writes the updated fieldsim.js, shipsim.js and
wpnsim.js. Run assemble.py afterwards.
"""
import base64
import os
import sys

if not os.path.exists("src/55_arms.js"):
    sys.exit("Abbruch: erst v158 einspielen.")
if "SEC_HOLD" in open("src/60_effects.js", encoding="utf-8").read():
    sys.exit("Abbruch: v159 ist schon eingespielt.")

F = {}
def load(p):
    if p not in F: F[p] = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
def rep(p, old, new, count=1):
    load(p)
    n = F[p].count(old)
    if n != count:
        sys.exit("Abbruch (%s): Suchtext %d-mal gefunden, erwartet %d.\n%s" % (p, n, count, old[:200]))
    F[p] = F[p].replace(old, new)

